WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:08.200
The first motorist to be fined for speeding
in the UK was Walter Arnold in 1896.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:20.750
He was doing 8 mph in a 2 mph zone.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:26.590
The average person who lives to be 75 will
have spent six years dreaming.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:32.949
In the first month of its life, a silkworm
puts on 10,000 times its birth weight.

00:00:32.949 --> 00:00:40.540
During World War II, the crew of the British
submarine HMS Trident kept a fully grown reindeer

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:46.780
called Pollyanna aboard their vessel for six
weeks (it was a gift from the Russians).

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:53.520
In 1999, a four-year-old girl turned yellow
after drinking too much Sunny Delight.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.200
Young Neanderthal girls had bigger biceps
than an adult male human.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:09.130
25 million Bibles were printed in 2011, compared
to 208 million IKEA catalogues.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:14.040
The longest hangover in medical literature
lasted four weeks.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.569
It belonged to a 37-year-old man from Glasgow.

00:01:18.569 --> 00:01:25.619
The katzenklavier or “cat piano”, was
a musical instrument made out of cats.

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:33.319
Designed by 17th-century German scholar Athanasius
Kircher, it consisted of a row of caged cats

00:01:33.319 --> 00:01:39.099
with different voice pitches, who could be
“played” by a keyboardist driving nails

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:41.469
into their tails.

00:01:41.469 --> 00:01:48.679
The ties bought in America for Father's Day
each year would stretch from New York to Rome.

00:01:48.679 --> 00:01:55.329
The Vatican City has the highest crime rate
in the world in comparison to its population.

00:01:55.329 --> 00:02:02.380
Though the resident population is only just
over 800, more than 600 crimes are committed

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.429
there each year.

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:10.569
Diagnosed with pleurisy, Sir Robert Chesebrough,
the inventor of Vaseline, decided to coat

00:02:10.569 --> 00:02:13.360
himself in his product from head to foot.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.930
He survived and lived to be 96.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:23.870
The world's lightest metal is 100 times lighter
than styrofoam and can rest on a dandelion

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.690
puff without damaging it.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:32.680
The symbols used by cartoonists to indicate
swearing are called grawlixes.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:38.870
Male fruit flies rejected by females drink
significantly more alcohol than those that

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:42.340
have had a successful mating encounter.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:45.970
Light doesn't always travel at the speed of
light.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:54.099
The slowest we've ever recorded light traveling
at is 38mph.

